# Whitelist strategy: ignore everything, track only durable configuration.
# Claude Code writes runtime state (sessions, history, caches, credentials)
# directly into this directory — none of that belongs in version control.
/*

# Tracked configuration.
# IMPORTANT: because everything is ignored by default, any NEW top-level file or
# directory must be added here or git will drop it silently — no error, and
# `git status` stays clean. Verify with: git status --ignored
!/.gitignore
!/LICENSE
!/README.md
!/CLAUDE.md

# Skills are whitelisted by name: re-include skills/ itself, re-exclude its
# children, then name the tracked ones. (A child cannot be re-included while
# its parent directory is excluded, so all three steps are required.)
# Unlisted directories under skills/ — e.g. installed third-party skills —
# stay untracked. A new skill written here needs its own line below.
!/skills/
/skills/*
!/skills/architecture-review/
!/skills/bug-fix/
!/skills/code-quality-review/
!/skills/debugging/
!/skills/security-audit/
!/skills/testing/

# Config surfaces not used yet; listed so they are tracked the day they appear.
!/commands/
!/agents/
!/output-styles/

# Never track local-only or generated files even inside tracked dirs
settings.local.json
.DS_Store
